{{/*
family: web-ui
what: poll
transports: v2c, v3
reference: RFC 3416 (SNMP operations), RFC 3414 (SNMPv3 users)
verification: reference
*/}}
{{define "does"}}The values to enter in the device's SNMP agent page so Woodshed can poll it (SNMP{{.Transport}}, read-only).{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part steps - In the device's web page, open its SNMP agent settings and enter
SNMP agent: on
SNMP version: {{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}v2c{{else}}v3{{end}}
{{- if eq .Transport "v2c"}}
Read-only community: <COMMUNITY>
{{- else}}
User name: {{.V3User}}
Security level: authentication and privacy (authPriv)
Authentication: {{.Auth.Label}}, passphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
Privacy: {{.Priv.Label}}, passphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
Access: read-only
{{- end}}
Allowed managers (if asked): {{.Address}}
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
{{if eq .Transport "v3"}}Add the same user in Woodshed: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, with the same name, protocols and passphrases.
{{end}}
Then add the device in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, SNMP{{.Transport}}{{if eq .Transport "v2c"}} and the same community{{else}} and the user {{.V3User}}{{end}}.
Field names differ between devices; some also need SNMP allowed on the interface Woodshed reaches.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with the device's name and interfaces.{{end}}
